{"id":"xbox-elite-v2","name":"Xbox Elite Wireless Controller Series 2","vendor":"Microsoft","vid":"0x045E","pid":"0x0B00","productString":"Controller","manufacturerString":"Microsoft","type":"gamepad","connection":"usb","descriptor":"","inputReportSize":null,"notes":"262-byte XboxGIP HID descriptor (USB/Windows view). See xbox-elite-v2-bt for 1038-byte Bluetooth descriptor with paddles, IMU, media controls. BT PIDs: 0x0B05, 0x0B22. Extended from 10 to 14 buttons (padding 6b to 2b, 16-bit envelope unchanged) so the four rear paddles land at descriptor buttons 11-14 in P1/P2/P3/P4 order, the order SDL's Elite mapping uses (paddle1:b11,paddle3:b12,paddle2:b13,paddle4:b14 in SDL_gamepad.c) and the GIP unmapped-state bit order (SDL_hidapi_xboxone.c, 0x01/0x02/0x04/0x08 at byte 14). Real hardware never exposes paddles in ANY HID view (USB is a vendor FF-class interface, paddles ride GIP unmapped-state messages; BLE uses Consumer Assign Selection 0x0C/0x81), so a declared-button carrier is the only HID-visible representation, the same call issue #50 made for the Series Share button.","deviceDescription":"HID-compliant game controller","triggerMode":"separate","driverMode":"xinputhid","layout":{"kind":"gamepad","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xbox_Wireless_Controller#Elite_controller","sticks":[{"side":"left","xAxis":"X","yAxis":"Y","clickButton":8},{"side":"right","xAxis":"Rx","yAxis":"Ry","clickButton":9}],"triggers":[{"axis":"Z","side":"left","kind":"analog"},{"axis":"Rz","side":"right","kind":"analog"}],"dpad":{"encoding":"hat","hatAxis":"Hat","hatPositions":8},"faceButtons":[{"role":"face_a","buttonIndex":0},{"role":"face_b","buttonIndex":1},{"role":"face_x","buttonIndex":2},{"role":"face_y","buttonIndex":3}],"shoulderButtons":[{"role":"left_bumper","buttonIndex":4},{"role":"right_bumper","buttonIndex":5}],"systemButtons":[{"role":"view","buttonIndex":6},{"role":"menu","buttonIndex":7}],"haptics":{"rumble":"impulse_triggers","triggerHaptics":true},"extraButtons